{
  "notes": {
    "event": "The React callback belongs to a React-only API or is named after the React convention while the element dispatches the documented minerva-* event (onDropdownVisibleChange / onClose -> minerva-open-change, onOptionClick / onItemSelect -> minerva-select, Pagination onChange -> minerva-page-change, CodeBlock onCopied -> minerva-copy with detail.success, onCopied being named so it does not replace the native onCopy); onPaletteChange follows ConfigProvider's setPalette(), which <minerva-config> does not have (the palette is its attribute).",
    "react-only": "React composition or styling hooks with no custom-element equivalent (ReactNode props without a slot of the same name are slots named differently, e.g. startIcon -> slot start; per-part style objects are ::part() selectors; data props that are children elements in HTML, e.g. KeyValueEditor entries -> value).",
    "wc-only": "Element vocabulary: string attributes replacing ReactNode props (heading, label, description, text), attributes replacing React context / provider values (locale, dialogRole, closeLabel...), state the element reflects for styling (collapsed, mobile, open on items), native-like properties React gets from the DOM element it renders (required, disabled, readOnly, placeholder, minLength, maxLength, autocomplete, href, target, rel, download, type, value).",
    "date-picker": "DatePicker uses hide-clear-button as the HTML boolean inverse of React clearable. The host id identifies the custom element and its associated label; React id identifies the inner input. The element additionally exposes open for imperative popup control and a read-only valueAsDate for local Date conversion."
  },
